  "ai_show_review": {
    "summary": "Smokin' 1982 Iowa City show – fire‑breathing Bertha, China>Rider & soaring Eyes",
    "review": "The August 10, 1982 Fieldhouse gig is one of the high‑water marks of the early‑’80s era. From the opening “Feel Like a Stranger” through a blistering first set that builds to an explosive “Bertha,” the band is locked in, delivering jaw‑dropping solos and tight group dynamics. The second set is fire‑breathing: a seamless China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider launch into a marathon Lost Sailor > Saint of Circumstance > Eyes of the World that showcases Jerry’s lyrical yet breakneck lead work, Phil’s thunderous low‑end “bombs,” and Brent Mydland’s soaring B3 textures and his prophetic vocal on “Iko Iko.” The night rolls forward with a powerhouse “Stagger Lee,” a joyous “Sugar Magnolia,” and a rare double encore that caps the energy at a perfect peak. Multiple excellent soundboard and matrix sources capture every nuance, making this show both an essential listen for completists and a pure joy for any Deadhead who loves high‑energy improvisation.",
